cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use fwhFoam in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "fwhFoam: A permeable/impermeable Ffowcs Williams–Hawkings acoustic solver for OpenFOAM"
abstract: >-
  fwhFoam is an open-source Ffowcs Williams–Hawkings (FW-H) acoustic-analogy
  solver for OpenFOAM. It implements Farassat's formulation 1A with a
  source-time-dominant (advanced-time) algorithm for both permeable and
  impermeable integration surfaces through a single unified code path, and
  supports a uniform mean flow via a closed-form Garrick-triangle emission-time
  relation. It provides a runtime function object, an offline reprocessing
  utility, Python companion tools, and an analytic verification suite.
type: software
authors:
